From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Configure the Cocoa port for armv7 and iOS 6 with CMake

The port is built by CMake as PORT=Cocoa with WEBKIT_IOS6 on, for an armv7
iPhone 4S on iOS 6.1.3, by a package recipe outside this tree rather than by
Xcode. This gives that build what it needs:

- OptionsIOS6.cmake: the feature set this device can run, and OptionsCocoa
  and WebKitMacros reading it;
- FindICU and FindWOFF2 that take the libraries from a package instead of the
  SDK, copy WebKit's ICU headers only into the folder its own finder makes, and
  find the WOFF2 common library and the compiler builtins;
- libxml2 and libxslt provided by a package to a Cocoa build;
- WebKitLegacy linked with the port's export list, frameworks given the
  Info.plist the port processed, and framework roots searched at link time in
  the order CMake finds them;
- the source lists and platform files of JavaScriptCore, WTF, WebCore,
  WebKitLegacy, bmalloc and ANGLE that name the port's sources;
- the includes a file needs when the unified sources group differently, so a
  build does not depend on which bundle a file happens to land in.
